  "id": "COMPOUND:11458 - PROTEIN:5845",
  "verbalization": "Flumedroxone is implicated in the biological pathway leading to SNU1 through a series of target interactions. The evidence suggests that Flumedroxone acts as a target for Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Ajugaciliatin E and Teyin. These compounds are all linked to SNU1, indicating a potential downstream effect of Flumedroxone on SNU1 through the SDR family. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Flumedroxone influences the activity of SDR family members, which then interact with SNU1. The recurring involvement of the SDR family suggests a common biological function or pathway that is modulated by Flumedroxone. The evidence supports a relationship between Flumedroxone and SNU1 through a chain of targets, emphasizing the role of the SDR family in mediating this interaction.",
